    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the repo has a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city owner capacity rule for `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is now rejected with **409** when the target city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in AGENTS.md, I added:\n\n1. **`RequireCityCapacity`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a step that reads the request DTO (`@Val OwnerFieldsDto`), counts existing owners in the same city case-insensitively via `OwnerRepository.findAll()`, and throws a checked `CityAtCapacityException` when the count is \u2265 50. The new owner isn't persisted yet, so all matches are existing owners.\n2. **`CityAtCapacityException`** \u2014 checked exception (mirrors `DuplicateHouseholdException`).\n3. **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds 409 with an `{\"errors\": [\"city\"]}` body, matching the existing conflict-handler shape.\n4. **Escalation YAML** `.../escalation/\u2026CityAtCapacityException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n5. Wired a `capacity` step into `owners.POST.yml` between the household-uniqueness and email steps, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).",
